  <tag k="comment" v="This relation has reached more than 2000 members and should be split in parts using a superroute as master."/>
  <tag k="e-road:class" v="A-intermediate"/>
  <tag k="name" v="European route E 54 (Germany)"/>
  <tag k="name:de" v="Europastraße 54"/>
  <tag k="name:en" v="European route E 54 (Germany)"/>
  <tag k="name:fr" v="E 54"/>
  <tag k="name:nl" v="Europese route E54 (Duitsland)"/>
  <tag k="name:sk" v="Európska cesta E 54 (Nemecko)"/>
  <tag k="network" v="e-road"/>
  <tag k="note:1" v="JOSM has problems showing the sequence of forward/backward ways, when they do not start at a common node. It does not have problems when ending in suche an open way."/>
  <tag k="note:2" v="Because both sides of E53 start with such separate roads, this problem is unavoidable. By reverting the whole route it can be seen, that the route ist sorted."/>
  <tag k="note:3" v="Links, which somewhere in between of the route and offer just a short connection to another road, are positioned in the relation near to near ways of the main route. They get the role &quot;link&quot;"/>
  <tag k="note:4" v="It's known that link is not an official role, but it is seen as the only way to handle this short &quot;dead ends&quot; (dead end with respect to the main route)."/>
  <tag k="ref" v="E 54"/>
  <tag k="route" v="road"/>
  <tag k="type" v="route"/>
  <tag k="wikidata" v="Q664865"/>
  <tag k="wikipedia" v="en:European route E54"/>
 </relation>
